    "question": "For every bike Henry sells, he is paid $8 more than he is paid to paint the bike. If Henry gets $5 to paint the bike, how much does he get paid to sell and paint 8 bikes?",
    "gold": "144",
    "answer": "Henry gets paid 5 + 13 = $<<5+13=18>>18 for each bike painted and sold.\nIn total, Henry will be paid 8 * 18 = $<<8*18=144>>144 for painting and selling 8 bikes.\n#### 144"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much Henry gets paid to sell and paint 8 bikes, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine how much Henry is paid to sell one bike.\n2. Calculate the total payment for selling 8 bikes.\n3. Calculate the total payment for painting 8 bikes.\n4. Add the two amounts together to get the total payment for selling and painting 8 bikes.\n\nStep 1: Determine how much Henry is paid to sell one bike.\nHenry is paid $8 more to sell a bike than to paint it. Since he gets $5 to paint one bike, he gets:\n\\[ 5 + 8 = 13 \\text{ dollars to sell one bike} \\]\n\nStep 2: Calculate the total payment for selling 8 bikes.\nIf Henry gets $13 to sell one bike, then for 8 bikes, he gets:\n\\[ 13 \\times 8 = 104 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nStep 3: Calculate the total payment for painting 8 bikes.\nSince Henry gets $5 to paint one bike, then for 8 bikes, he gets:\n\\[ 5 \\times 8 = 40 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nStep 4: Add the two amounts together to get the total payment for selling and painting 8 bikes.\nThe total payment is:\n\\[ 104 + 40 = 144 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{144} \\]",
